From e0c7afb967574cf7693a9eff5a6cb468db4aa61d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 12:39:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/29] Ask the loader for instance entry points with an
 instance, and fix the device struct

The probe blocked every launch on the phone with "the loader has no
vkDestroyInstance". The loader was right: with instance = NULL it only has to
answer the handful of global commands, and vkDestroyInstance is not one of them.
vkCreateInstance is now resolved as a global command and everything else after
the instance exists, using its handle - with a second attempt at NULL, because
loaders differ in how strictly they draw that line.

The second bug is worse and was invisible: VkPhysicalDeviceProperties begins
with sType and pNext, and this struct left them out, so every field was read 16
bytes low. The device name came back as the driver version followed by the
vendor id, which means the check that is supposed to prove the right driver
answered was reading nonsense and could never have named a Mali-G615.

Both would have been caught by running the probe once, so it is now run. A fake
Vulkan loader (tools/test/mock_vulkan.c - gcc and python3, nothing destined for
the phone) answers NULL for instance commands until an instance exists, reports
a Mali-G615 MC6, performs the fill for real, and can be told what the fence
says. Five cases - a passing run, the device name, a fence that never signals,
a fence that lies about the work, and no loader at all - run in the build before
the app is compiled.

Co-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
